  "problem": "Consider the frequency table below for a continuous variable $x.$ The total number of observations is $n=15,$ and the estimated sample mean is $\\overset{―}{x}≈23.$\n\n| Range | Frequency $({f}_{i})$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $0\\le x<10$ | $2$ |\n| $10\\le x<20$ | $4$ |\n| $20\\le x<30$ | $4$ |\n| $30\\le x<40$ | $5$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nUsing the midpoint of each class interval to approximate all observations within that class, estimate the standard deviation ${\\sigma }_{n},$ using $n$ as the denominator in the variance formula.\n\nRounded to one decimal place, ${\\sigma }_{n}≈$\n{{field-1}}",
